commands
========

The implementations of Pyxplot's commands. The parser (src/parser) matches each
command line against the command definitions, and parserExecute.c calls the
ppl_directive_* function here which implements it. Plotting commands are in
src/epsMaker and canvasItems.c.

core.c, core.h
    Simple commands: assert, cd, exec, global, history, load, local, print and
    save, and variable assignment, including the =~ operator which applies a
    sed regular expression to a string.

eqnsolve.c, eqnsolve.h
    The solve, minimise and maximise commands, which vary free variables with
    GSL's simplex minimiser to solve equations or find extrema.

fft.c, fft.h
    The fft and ifft commands, which Fourier transform gridded data from a file
    or a function with FFTW, and store the result as a new function.

fit.c, fit.h
    The fit command, which fits a function to data by maximum likelihood, and
    estimates the uncertainties of the fitted parameters from the Hessian
    matrix.

flowctrl.c, flowctrl.h
    Flow control: the do, for, foreach, foreach datum and while loops, if
    statements, with blocks, subroutine definitions, and break, continue and
    return.

funcset.c, funcset.h
    Function definitions such as f(x)=x**2, which may be restricted to ranges
    of their arguments, so that a function can be defined piecewise.

help.c, help.h
    The help command, which finds the requested topic in the XML help document
    and displays it through a pager.

histogram.c, histogram.h
    The histogram command, which bins data from a file and stores the result as
    a new function.

interpolate.c, interpolate.h
    The interpolate command, which stores a new function interpolating between
    data points from a file or the pixels of a bitmap image, in one or two
    dimensions.

interpolate_2d_engine.c, interpolate_2d_engine.h
    Two-dimensional interpolation of scattered data onto a regular grid, used
    by the interpolate command and by plot styles which need gridded data.

set.c, set.h
    The set and unset commands, which change Pyxplot's settings, or those of a
    multiplot item.

show.c, show.h
    The show command, which lists the values of settings in the syntax of the
    set commands which would set them, along with variables, functions and
    units.

tabulate.c, tabulate.h
    The tabulate command, which writes data from files or functions to a text
    file, in the same way that the plot command would plot it.
